    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0203" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg115"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1535.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a decree which was issued by the Emperor the 21st instant. This
                    decree may be taken in some sense as an answer to my late request that strenuous
                    action be taken with regard to the “Hu-Nan publications,” a copy whereof was
                    inclosed in my dispatch No, 1514 of April 12. It will be seen that the Taotai
                    Chou Han who was supposed to be chief circulator of the “Hu-Nan publications”
                    has been degraded. He is to be sent to his native place and kept under
                    surveillance.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d85-a1.xml" xpointer="d85-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
